{
  "summary": "While the combined CSS selector fix is correct in principle, there are several weaknesses worth noting: (1) The tests use FakeApp/MagicMock objects that don't actually verify Textual's query() returns DOM-ordered results with comma-separated selectors—they only test the navigation logic given a pre-ordered list, so if Textual's behavior changes or differs across versions, the tests won't catch it. (2) The bare `except Exception` around `query_one('#items-pane')` silently swallows errors and continues to navigate even when the items pane doesn't exist, which could cause confusing behavior in edge cases. (3) The `current in item_list` check uses identity/equality on Textual widgets, and the redundant try/except ValueError after already confirming membership is dead code. Despite these minor issues, the core fix is sound and the bug can reasonably be considered resolved."
}
